When editing of an item starts, this function is called with the *event* that triggered
the editing, the *model*, the *index* of the item, and the *option* used for rendering
the item.

Mouse events are sent to editorEvent() even if they don't start editing of the item.
This can, for instance, be useful if you wish to open a context menu when the right
mouse button is pressed on an item.

The base implementation returns `false` (indicating that it has not handled the event).

