### `[virtual protected]` [QAbstractSpinBox::StepEnabled](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qabstractspinbox.html#StepEnabledFlag-enum) QAbstractSpinBox::stepEnabled() const

Virtual function that determines whether stepping up and down is legal at any given
time.

The up arrow will be painted as disabled unless (stepEnabled() \\&
[StepUpEnabled](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qabstractspinbox.html#StepEnabledFlag-enum))
!\\= 0\\.

The default implementation will return
([StepUpEnabled](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qabstractspinbox.html#StepEnabledFlag-enum)\\|
[StepDownEnabled](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qabstractspinbox.html#StepEnabledFlag-enum))
if wrapping is turned on. Else it will return
[StepDownEnabled](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qabstractspinbox.html#StepEnabledFlag-enum)
if value is \\> minimum() or'ed with
[StepUpEnabled](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qabstractspinbox.html#StepEnabledFlag-enum)
if value \\< maximum().

If you subclass
[QAbstractSpinBox](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qabstractspinbox.html) you will
need to reimplement this function.

**See also**
[QSpinBox::minimum](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qspinbox.html#minimum-prop)(),
[QSpinBox::maximum](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qspinbox.html#maximum-prop)(),
and
[wrapping](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qabstractspinbox.html#wrapping-prop)().

