    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### iconText : [QString](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstring.html)\n\nThis property holds the action's descriptive icon text\n\nIf\n[QToolBar::toolButtonStyle](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtoolbar.html#toolButtonStyle-prop)\nis set to a value that permits text to be displayed, the text defined held in this\nproperty appears as a label in the relevant tool button.\n\nIt also serves as the default text in menus and tooltips if the action has not been\ndefined with [setText](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#text-prop)() or\n[setToolTip](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#toolTip-prop)(), and will\nalso be used in toolbar buttons if no icon has been defined using\n[setIcon](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#icon-prop)().\n\nIf the icon text is not explicitly set, the action's normal text will be used for the\nicon text.\n\nBy default, this property contains an empty string.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QString | **iconText**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setIconText**(const QString \\&*text*) |\n\n**Notifier signal:**\n\n| void | **[changed](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#changed)**() |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also**\n[setToolTip](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#toolTip-prop)() and\n[setStatusTip](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#statusTip-prop)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#iconText"
