    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### dateTime : [QDateTime](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetime.html)\n\nThis property holds the [QDateTime](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetime.html)\nthat is set in the\n[QDateTimeEdit](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetimeedit.html).\n\nWhen setting this property the timespec of the\n[QDateTimeEdit](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetimeedit.html) remains the same\nand the timespec of the new\n[QDateTime](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetime.html) is ignored.\n\nBy default, this property is set to the start of 2000 CE. It can only be set to a valid\n[QDateTime](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetime.html) value. If any operation\ncauses this property to have an invalid date-time as value, it is reset to the value of\nthe\n[minimumDateTime](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetimeedit.html#minimumDateTime-prop)\nproperty.\n\nIf the [QDateTimeEdit](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetimeedit.html) has no\ndate fields, setting this property sets the widget's date-range to start and end on the\ndate of the new value of this property.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QDateTime | **dateTime**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setDateTime**(const QDateTime \\&*dateTime*) |\n\n**Notifier signal:**\n\n| void | **[dateTimeChanged](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetimeedit.html#dateTimeChanged)**(const QDateTime \\&*datetime*) |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also** [date](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetimeedit.html#date),\n[time](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetimeedit.html#time),\n[minimumDateTime](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetimeedit.html#minimumDateTime-prop),\nand\n[maximumDateTime](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetimeedit.html#maximumDateTime-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatetimeedit.html#dateTime"
