### int QFileDevice::handle() const

Returns the file handle of the file.

This is a small positive integer, suitable for use with C library functions such as
`fdopen()` and `fcntl()`. On systems that use file descriptors for sockets (i.e. Unix
systems, but not Windows) the handle can be used with
[QSocketNotifier](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsocketnotifier.html) as well.

If the file is not open, or there is an error, handle() returns -1.

