    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### sceneRect : [QRectF](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qrectf.html)\n\nThis property holds the scene rectangle; the bounding rectangle of the scene\n\nThe scene rectangle defines the extent of the scene. It is primarily used by\n[QGraphicsView](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html) to determine the\nview's default scrollable area, and by\n[QGraphicsScene](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsscene.html) to manage item\nindexing.\n\nIf unset, or if set to a null [QRectF](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qrectf.html),\nsceneRect() will return the largest bounding rect of all items on the scene since the\nscene was created (i.e., a rectangle that grows when items are added to or moved in the\nscene, but never shrinks).\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QRectF | **sceneRect**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setSceneRect**(const QRectF \\&*rect*) |\n| void | **setSceneRect**(qreal *x*, qreal *y*, qreal *w*, qreal *h*) |\n\n**See also** [width](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsscene.html#width)(),\n[height](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsscene.html#height)(), and\n[QGraphicsView::sceneRect](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#sceneRect-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsscene.html#sceneRect"
