    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### alignment : [Qt::Alignment](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AlignmentFlag-enum)\n\nThis property holds the alignment of the scene in the view when the whole scene is\nvisible.\n\nIf the whole scene is visible in the view, (i.e., there are no visible scroll bars,) the\nview's alignment will decide where the scene will be rendered in the view. For example,\nif the alignment is\n[Qt::AlignCenter](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AlignmentFlag-enum), which\nis default, the scene will be centered in the view, and if the alignment is\n([Qt::AlignLeft](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AlignmentFlag-enum) \\|\n[Qt::AlignTop](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AlignmentFlag-enum)), the\nscene will be rendered in the top-left corner of the view.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| Qt::Alignment | **alignment**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setAlignment**(Qt::Alignment *alignment*) |\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#alignment"
