    backgroundBrush: QBrush
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### backgroundBrush : [QBrush](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qbrush.html)\n\nThis property holds the background brush of the scene.\n\nThis property sets the background brush for the scene in this view. It is used to\noverride the scene's own background, and defines the behavior of\n[drawBackground](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#drawBackground)().\nTo provide custom background drawing for this view, you can reimplement\n[drawBackground](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#drawBackground)()\ninstead.\n\nBy default, this property contains a brush with the\n[Qt::NoBrush](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#BrushStyle-enum) pattern.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QBrush | **backgroundBrush**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setBackgroundBrush**(const QBrush \\&*brush*) |\n\n**See also**\n[QGraphicsScene::backgroundBrush](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsscene.html#backgroundBrush-prop)\nand\n[foregroundBrush](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#foregroundBrush-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#backgroundBrush"
    baseSize: QSize
    cacheMode: Any
    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### cacheMode : [CacheMode](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#CacheModeFlag-enum)\n\nThis property holds which parts of the view are cached\n\n[QGraphicsView](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html) can cache\npre-rendered content in a [QPixmap](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpixmap.html),\nwhich is then drawn onto the viewport. The purpose of such caching is to speed up the\ntotal rendering time for areas that are slow to render. Texture, gradient and alpha\nblended backgrounds, for example, can be notibly slow to render; especially with a\ntransformed view. The\n[CacheBackground](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#CacheModeFlag-enum)\nflag enables caching of the view\'s background. For example:\n\n```\nQGraphicsView view;\nview.setBackgroundBrush(QImage(":/images/backgroundtile.png"));\nview.setCacheMode(QGraphicsView::CacheBackground);\n```\n\nThe cache is invalidated every time the view is transformed. However, when scrolling,\nonly partial invalidation is required.\n\nBy default, nothing is cached.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QGraphicsView::CacheMode | **cacheMode**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setCacheMode**(QGraphicsView::CacheMode *mode*) |\n\n**See also**\n[resetCachedContent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#resetCachedContent)()\nand [QPixmapCache](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpixmapcache.html).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#cacheMode'
