    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### optimizationFlags : [OptimizationFlags](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#OptimizationFlag-enum)\n\nflags that can be used to tune\n[QGraphicsView](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html)'s performance.\n\n[QGraphicsView](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html) uses clipping,\nextra bounding rect adjustments, and certain other aids to improve rendering quality and\nperformance for the common case graphics scene. However, depending on the target\nplatform, the scene, and the viewport in use, some of these operations can degrade\nperformance.\n\nThe effect varies from flag to flag; see the\n[OptimizationFlags](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#OptimizationFlag-enum)\ndocumentation for details.\n\nBy default, no optimization flags are enabled.\n\nThis property was introduced in Qt 4.3.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QGraphicsView::OptimizationFlags | **optimizationFlags**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setOptimizationFlags**(QGraphicsView::OptimizationFlags *flags*) |\n\n**See also**\n[setOptimizationFlag](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#setOptimizationFlag)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#optimizationFlags"
