    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### renderHints : [QPainter::RenderHints](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpainter.html#RenderHint-enum)\n\nThis property holds the default render hints for the view\n\nThese hints are used to initialize\n[QPainter](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpainter.html) before each visible item is\ndrawn. [QPainter](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpainter.html) uses render hints to\ntoggle rendering features such as antialiasing and smooth pixmap transformation.\n\n[QPainter::TextAntialiasing](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpainter.html#RenderHint-enum)\nis enabled by default.\n\nExample:\n\n```\nQGraphicsScene scene;\nscene.addRect(QRectF(-10, -10, 20, 20));\n\nQGraphicsView view(&scene);\nview.setRenderHints(QPainter::Antialiasing | QPainter::SmoothPixmapTransform);\nview.show();\n```\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QPainter::RenderHints | **renderHints**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setRenderHints**(QPainter::RenderHints *hints*) |\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#renderHints'
    resizeAnchor: Any
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### resizeAnchor : [ViewportAnchor](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#ViewportAnchor-enum)\n\nhow the view should position the scene when the view is resized.\n\n[QGraphicsView](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html) uses this\nproperty to decide how to position the scene in the viewport when the viewport widget's\nsize changes. The default behavior,\n[NoAnchor](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#ViewportAnchor-enum),\nleaves the scene's position unchanged during a resize; the top-left corner of the view\nwill appear to be anchored while resizing.\n\nNote that the effect of this property is noticeable when only a part of the scene is\nvisible (i.e., when there are scroll bars). Otherwise, if the whole scene fits in the\nview, [QGraphicsScene](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsscene.html) uses the\nview [alignment](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/stylesheet-reference.html#alignment)\nto position the scene in the view.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QGraphicsView::ViewportAnchor | **resizeAnchor**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setResizeAnchor**(QGraphicsView::ViewportAnchor *anchor*) |\n\n**See also**\n[alignment](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/stylesheet-reference.html#alignment) and\n[transformationAnchor](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#transformationAnchor-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#resizeAnchor"
    rubberBandSelectionMode: Any
    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### rubberBandSelectionMode : [Qt::ItemSelectionMode](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#ItemSelectionMode-enum)\n\nThis property holds the behavior for selecting items with a rubber band selection\nrectangle.\n\nThis property defines how items are selected when using the\n[RubberBandDrag](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#DragMode-enum)\ndrag mode.\n\nThe default value is\n[Qt::IntersectsItemShape](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#ItemSelectionMode-enum);\nall items whose shape intersects with or is contained by the rubber band are selected.\n\nThis property was introduced in Qt 4.3.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| Qt::ItemSelectionMode | **rubberBandSelectionMode**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setRubberBandSelectionMode**(Qt::ItemSelectionMode *mode*) |\n\n**See also**\n[dragMode](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#dragMode-prop),\n[items](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#items)(), and\n[rubberBandRect](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#rubberBandRect)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#rubberBandSelectionMode'
    sceneRect: QRectF
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### sceneRect : [QRectF](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qrectf.html)\n\nThis property holds the area of the scene visualized by this view.\n\nThe scene rectangle defines the extent of the scene, and in the view's case, this means\nthe area of the scene that you can navigate using the scroll bars.\n\nIf unset, or if a null [QRectF](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qrectf.html) is set,\nthis property has the same value as\n[QGraphicsScene::sceneRect](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsscene.html#sceneRect-prop),\nand it changes with\n[QGraphicsScene::sceneRect](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsscene.html#sceneRect-prop).\nOtherwise, the view's scene rect is unaffected by the scene.\n\nNote that, although the scene supports a virtually unlimited size, the range of the\nscroll bars will never exceed the range of an integer (INT\\_MIN, INT\\_MAX). When the\nscene is larger than the scroll bars' values, you can choose to use\n[translate](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#translate)() to\nnavigate the scene instead.\n\nBy default, this property contains a rectangle at the origin with zero width and height.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QRectF | **sceneRect**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setSceneRect**(const QRectF \\&*rect*) |\n| void | **setSceneRect**(qreal *x*, qreal *y*, qreal *w*, qreal *h*) |\n\n**See also**\n[QGraphicsScene::sceneRect](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsscene.html#sceneRect-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsview.html#sceneRect"
