### `[slot]` bool QGraphicsWidget::close()

Call this function to close the widget.

Returns `true` if the widget was closed; otherwise returns `false`. This slot will first
send a [QCloseEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcloseevent.html) to the widget,
which may or may not accept the event. If the event was ignored, nothing happens. If the
event was accepted, it will
[hide](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsitem.html#hide)() the widget.

If the widget has the
[Qt::WA\\_DeleteOnClose](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WidgetAttribute-enum)
attribute set it will be deleted.

