### void QGraphicsWidget::setContentsMargins([QMarginsF](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qmarginsf.html) *margins*)

Sets the widget's contents margins to *margins*.

Contents margins are used by the assigned layout to define the placement of subwidgets
and layouts. Margins are particularly useful for widgets that constrain subwidgets to
only a section of its own geometry. For example, a group box with a layout will place
subwidgets inside its frame, but below the title.

