### `[virtual protected]` [Qt::WindowFrameSection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WindowFrameSection-enum) QGraphicsWidget::windowFrameSectionAt(const [QPointF](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpointf.html) \\&*pos*) const

Returns the window frame section at position *pos*, or
[Qt::NoSection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WindowFrameSection-enum) if
there is no window frame section at this position.

This function is used in
[QGraphicsWidget](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/graphicsview.html#qgraphicswidget)'s
base implementation for window frame interaction.

You can reimplement this function if you want to customize how a window can be
interactively moved or resized. For instance, if you only want to allow a window to be
resized by the bottom right corner, you can reimplement this function to return
[Qt::NoSection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WindowFrameSection-enum) for
all sections except
[Qt::BottomRightSection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WindowFrameSection-enum).

This function was introduced in Qt 4.4.

**See also**
[windowFrameEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicswidget.html#windowFrameEvent)(),
