### void QGridLayout::addLayout([QLayout](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlayout.html#QLayout) \\**layout*, int *row*, int *column*, [Qt::Alignment](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AlignmentFlag-enum) *alignment* \\= Qt::Alignment())

Places the *layout* at position (*row*, *column*) in the grid. The top-left position is
(0, 0).

The alignment is specified by *alignment*. The default alignment is 0, which means that
the widget fills the entire cell.

A non-zero alignment indicates that the layout should not grow to fill the available
space but should be sized according to
[sizeHint](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgridlayout.html#sizeHint)().

*layout* becomes a child of the grid layout.

