    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### flow : [Flow](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlistview.html#Flow-enum)\n\nThis property holds which direction the items layout should flow.\n\nIf this property is\n[LeftToRight](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlistview.html#Flow-enum), the items\nwill be laid out left to right. If the\n[isWrapping](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlistview.html#isWrapping-prop) property\nis `true`, the layout will wrap when it reaches the right side of the visible area. If\nthis property is\n[TopToBottom](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlistview.html#Flow-enum), the items\nwill be laid out from the top of the visible area, wrapping when it reaches the bottom.\n\nSetting this property when the view is visible will cause the items to be laid out\nagain.\n\nBy default, this property is set to\n[TopToBottom](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlistview.html#Flow-enum).\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QListView::Flow | **flow**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setFlow**(QListView::Flow *flow*) |\n\n**See also**\n[viewMode](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlistview.html#viewMode-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlistview.html#flow'
