### `[slot]` void QMdiSubWindow::showShaded()

Calling this function makes the subwindow enter the shaded mode. When the subwindow is
shaded, only the title bar is visible.

Although shading is not supported by all styles, this function will still show the
subwindow as shaded, regardless of whether support for shading is available. However,
when used with styles without shading support, the user will be unable to return from
shaded mode through the user interface (e.g., through a shade button in the title bar).

**See also**
[isShaded](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qmdisubwindow.html#isShaded)().

