### [QVector](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qvector.html)\\<float\\> QOpenGLShaderProgram::defaultInnerTessellationLevels() const

Returns the default inner tessellation levels to be used by the tessellation primitive
generator in the event that the tessellation control shader does not output them. For
more details on OpenGL and Tessellation shaders see [OpenGL Tessellation
Shaders](http://www.opengl.org/wiki/Tessellation_Shader).

Returns a [QVector](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qvector.html) of floats
describing the inner tessellation levels. The vector will always have two elements but
not all of them make sense for every mode of tessellation.

**Note:** This returns the global OpenGL state value. It is not specific to this
[QOpenGLShaderProgram](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopenglshaderprogram.html)
instance.

**Note:** This function is only supported with OpenGL \\>\\= 4.0 and will not return valid
results with OpenGL ES 3.2.

**See also**
[setDefaultInnerTessellationLevels](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopenglshaderprogram.html#setDefaultInnerTessellationLevels)()
and
[defaultOuterTessellationLevels](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopenglshaderprogram.html#defaultOuterTessellationLevels)().

