### void QOpenGLShaderProgram::setDefaultInnerTessellationLevels(const [QVector](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qvector.html)\\<float\\> \\&*levels*)

Sets the default outer tessellation levels to be used by the tessellation primitive
generator in the event that the tessellation control shader does not output them to
*levels*. For more details on OpenGL and Tessellation shaders see [OpenGL Tessellation
Shaders](http://www.opengl.org/wiki/Tessellation_Shader).

The *levels* argument should be a
[QVector](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qvector.html) consisting of 2 floats. Not
all of the values make sense for all tessellation modes. If you specify a vector with
fewer than 2 elements, the remaining elements will be given a default value of 1\\.

**Note:** This modifies global OpenGL state and is not specific to this
[QOpenGLShaderProgram](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopenglshaderprogram.html)
instance. You should call this in your render function when needed, as
[QOpenGLShaderProgram](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopenglshaderprogram.html)
will not apply this for you. This is purely a convenience function.

**Note:** This function is only available with OpenGL \\>\\= 4.0 and is not supported with
OpenGL ES 3.2.

**See also**
[defaultInnerTessellationLevels](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopenglshaderprogram.html#defaultInnerTessellationLevels)()
and
[setDefaultOuterTessellationLevels](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopenglshaderprogram.html#setDefaultOuterTessellationLevels)().

