### void QOpenGLShaderProgram::setPatchVertexCount(int *count*)

Use this function to specify to OpenGL the number of vertices in a patch to *count*. A
patch is a custom OpenGL primitive whose interpretation is entirely defined by the
tessellation shader stages. Therefore, calling this function only makes sense when using
a [QOpenGLShaderProgram](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopenglshaderprogram.html)
containing tessellation stage shaders. When using OpenGL tessellation, the only
primitive that can be rendered with `glDraw*()` functions is `GL_PATCHES`.

This is equivalent to calling glPatchParameteri(GL\\_PATCH\\_VERTICES, count).

**Note:** This modifies global OpenGL state and is not specific to this
[QOpenGLShaderProgram](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopenglshaderprogram.html)
instance. You should call this in your render function when needed, as
[QOpenGLShaderProgram](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopenglshaderprogram.html)
will not apply this for you. This is purely a convenience function.

**See also**
[patchVertexCount](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopenglshaderprogram.html#patchVertexCount)().

