### void QOpenGLTexture::setSize(int *width*, int *height* \\= 1, int *depth* \\= 1\\)

Sets the dimensions of this texture object to *width*, *height*, and *depth*. The
default for each dimension is 1\\. The maximum allowable texture size is dependent upon
your OpenGL implementation. Allocating storage for a texture less than the maximum size
can still fail if your system is low on resources.

If a non-power-of-two *width*, *height* or *depth* is provided and your OpenGL
implementation doesn't have support for repeating non-power-of-two textures, then the
wrap mode is automatically set to
[ClampToEdge](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopengltexture.html#WrapMode-enum).

