Native bases: PythonQtInstanceWrapper

Supplemental documentation:
Qt 5 reference:

## Detailed Description

QPaintDeviceWindow is like a regular
[QWindow](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwindow.html), with the added functionality
of being a paint device too. Whenever the content needs to be updated, the virtual
[paintEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpaintdevicewindow.html#paintEvent)()
function is called. Subclasses, that reimplement this function, can then simply open a
[QPainter](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpainter.html) on the window.

**Note:** This class cannot directly be used in applications. It rather serves as a base
for subclasses like
[QOpenGLWindow](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qopenglwindow.html).

Source: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpaintdevicewindow.html"""

