### bool QPixmap::save(const [QString](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstring.html) \\&*fileName*, const char \\**format* \\= nullptr, int *quality* \\= -1) const

Saves the pixmap to the file with the given *fileName* using the specified image file
*format* and *quality* factor. Returns `true` if successful; otherwise returns `false`.

The *quality* factor must be in the range \\[0,100\\] or -1. Specify 0 to obtain small
compressed files, 100 for large uncompressed files, and -1 to use the default settings.

If *format* is `nullptr`, an image format will be chosen from *fileName*'s suffix.

**See also** [Reading and Writing Image
Files](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpixmap.html#reading-and-writing-image-files).

