### `[slot]` void QProgressBar::setRange(int *minimum*, int *maximum*)

Sets the progress bar's minimum and maximum values to *minimum* and *maximum*
respectively.

If *maximum* is smaller than *minimum*, *minimum* becomes the only legal value.

If the current value falls outside the new range, the progress bar is reset with
[reset](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qprogressbar.html#reset)().

The [QProgressBar](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qprogressbar.html) can be set to
undetermined state by using setRange(0, 0).

**See also**
[minimum](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qprogressbar.html#minimum-prop) and
[maximum](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qprogressbar.html#maximum-prop).

