### void QPushButton::setMenu([QMenu](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qmenu.html) \\**menu*)

Associates the popup menu *menu* with this push button. This turns the button into a
menu button, which in some styles will produce a small triangle to the right of the
button's text.

Ownership of the menu is *not* transferred to the push button.

![Screenshot of a Fusion style push button with popup
menu.](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/images/fusion-pushbutton-menu.png)

A push button with popup menus shown in the [Fusion widget
style](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/gallery.html).

**See also** [menu](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpushbutton.html#menu)().

