    def advancesForGlyphIndexes(self, glyphIndexes: Any, advances: Any, numGlyphs: Any, layoutFlags: Any) -> tuple:
        """X.advancesForGlyphIndexes(glyphIndexes, advances, numGlyphs, layoutFlags) -> tuple

Supplemental documentation:
Qt 5 reference:

### [QVector](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qvector.html)\\<[QPointF](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpointf.html)\\> QRawFont::advancesForGlyphIndexes(const [QVector](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qvector.html)\\<[quint32](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtglobal.html#quint32-typedef)\\> \\&*glyphIndexes*, [QRawFont::LayoutFlags](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qrawfont.html#LayoutFlag-enum) *layoutFlags*) const

Returns the [QRawFont](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qrawfont.html)'s advances for
each of the *glyphIndexes* in pixel units. The advances give the distance from the
position of a given glyph to where the next glyph should be drawn to make it appear as
if the two glyphs are unspaced. How the advances are calculated is controlled by
*layoutFlags*.

This function was introduced in Qt 5.1.

**See also**
[QTextLine::horizontalAdvance](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtextline.html#horizontalAdvance)()
