### void QRect::translate(int *dx*, int *dy*)

Moves the rectangle *dx* along the x axis and *dy* along the y axis, relative to the
current position. Positive values move the rectangle to the right and down.

**See also** [moveTopLeft](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qrect.html#moveTopLeft)(),
[moveTo](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qrect.html#moveTo)(), and
[translated](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qrect.html#translated)().

### void QRect::translate(const [QPoint](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpoint.html) \\&*offset*)

This is an overloaded function.

Moves the rectangle *offset*.[x()](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpoint.html#x)
