Native bases: PythonQtInstanceWrapper

Supplemental documentation:
Qt 5 reference:

## Detailed Description

QSequentialAnimationGroup is a
[QAnimationGroup](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qanimationgroup.html) that runs its
animations in sequence, i.e., it starts one animation after another has finished
playing. The animations are played in the order they are added to the group (using
[addAnimation()](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qanimationgroup.html#addAnimation)
or
[insertAnimation()](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qanimationgroup.html#insertAnimation)).
The animation group finishes when its last animation has finished.

At each moment there is at most one animation that is active in the group; it is
returned by
[currentAnimation](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsequentialanimationgroup.html#currentAnimation-prop)().
An empty group has no current animation.

A sequential animation group can be treated as any other animation, i.e., it can be
started, stopped, and added to other groups. You can also call
[addPause](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsequentialanimationgroup.html#addPause)()
or
[insertPause](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsequentialanimationgroup.html#insertPause)()
to add a pause to a sequential animation group.

```
    QSequentialAnimationGroup *group = new QSequentialAnimationGroup;

    group->addAnimation(anim1);
    group->addAnimation(anim2);

    group->start();
```

In this example, `anim1` and `anim2` are two already set up
[QPropertyAnimation](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpropertyanimation.html)s.

Source: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsequentialanimationgroup.html"""

