### void QSize::scale(int *width*, int *height*, [Qt::AspectRatioMode](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AspectRatioMode-enum) *mode*)

Scales the size to a rectangle with the given *width* and *height*, according to the
specified *mode*:

- If *mode* is [Qt::IgnoreAspectRatio](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AspectRatioMode-enum), the size is set to (*width*, *height*).
- If *mode* is [Qt::KeepAspectRatio](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AspectRatioMode-enum), the current size is scaled to a rectangle as large as possible inside (*width*, *height*), preserving the aspect ratio.
