### `[slot]` void QSplashScreen::showMessage(const [QString](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstring.html) \\&*message*, int *alignment* \\= Qt::AlignLeft, const [QColor](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcolor.html) \\&*color* \\= Qt::black)

Draws the *message* text onto the splash screen with color *color* and aligns the text
according to the flags in *alignment*. This function calls
[repaint](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsplashscreen.html#repaint)() to make sure
the splash screen is repainted immediately. As a result the message is kept up to date
with what your application is doing (e.g. loading files).

**See also**
[Qt::Alignment](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AlignmentFlag-enum),
[clearMessage](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsplashscreen.html#clearMessage)(),
