The QStyleOptionToolBar class holds the
[lineWidth](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstyleoptiontoolbar.html#lineWidth-var)
and the
[midLineWidth](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstyleoptiontoolbar.html#midLineWidth-var)
for drawing the widget. It also stores information about which
[area](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstyleoptiontoolbar.html#toolBarArea-var) the
toolbar should be located in, whether it is movable or not, which position the toolbar
line should have
([positionOfLine](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstyleoptiontoolbar.html#positionOfLine-var)),
and the toolbar's position within the line
([positionWithinLine](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstyleoptiontoolbar.html#positionWithinLine-var)).

In addition, the class provides a couple of enums: The
[ToolBarFeature](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstyleoptiontoolbar.html#ToolBarFeature-enum)
enum is used to describe whether a toolbar is movable or not, and the
[ToolBarPosition](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstyleoptiontoolbar.html#ToolBarPosition-enum)
enum is used to describe the position of a toolbar line, as well as the toolbar's
position within the line.

For an example demonstrating how style options can be used, see the
[Styles](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtwidgets-widgets-styles-example.html)
example.

