### bool QTemporaryDir::autoRemove() const

Returns `true` if the
[QTemporaryDir](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtemporarydir.html) is in auto remove
mode. Auto-remove mode will automatically delete the directory from disk upon
destruction. This makes it very easy to create your
[QTemporaryDir](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtemporarydir.html) object on the
stack, fill it with files, do something with the files, and finally on function return
it will automatically clean up after itself.

Auto-remove is on by default.

**See also**
[setAutoRemove](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtemporarydir.html#setAutoRemove)()
and [remove](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtemporarydir.html#remove)().

