### `[virtual protected]` void QWidget::closeEvent([QCloseEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcloseevent.html) \\**event*)

This event handler is called with the given *event* when Qt receives a window close
request for a top-level widget from the window system.

By default, the event is accepted and the widget is closed. You can reimplement this
function to change the way the widget responds to window close requests. For example,
you can prevent the window from closing by calling
[ignore()](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qevent.html#ignore) on all events.

Main window applications typically use reimplementations of this function to check
whether the user's work has been saved and ask for permission before closing. For
example, the [Application
Example](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtwidgets-mainwindows-application-example.html)
uses a helper function to determine whether or not to close the window:

```
void MainWindow::closeEvent(QCloseEvent *event)
{
    if (maybeSave()) {
        writeSettings();
        event->accept();
    } else {
        event->ignore();
    }
}
```

