    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### frameSize : const [QSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsize.html)\n\nThis property holds the size of the widget including any window frame\n\nBy default, this property contains a value that depends on the user's platform and\nscreen geometry.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QSize | **frameSize**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#frameSize"
    fullScreen: Any
    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### fullScreen : const bool\n\nThis property holds whether the widget is shown in full screen mode\n\nA widget in full screen mode occupies the whole screen area and does not display window\ndecorations, such as a title bar.\n\nBy default, this property is `false`.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| bool | **isFullScreen**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also**\n[windowState](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#windowState)(),\n[minimized](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimized-prop), and\n[maximized](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximized-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#fullScreen'
    geometry: QRect
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### geometry : [QRect](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qrect.html)\n\nThis property holds the geometry of the widget relative to its parent and excluding the\nwindow frame\n\nWhen changing the geometry, the widget, if visible, receives a move event\n([moveEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#moveEvent)()) and/or a\nresize event\n([resizeEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#resizeEvent)())\nimmediately. If the widget is not currently visible, it is guaranteed to receive\nappropriate events before it is shown.\n\nThe size component is adjusted if it lies outside the range defined by\n[minimumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumSize-prop)() and\n[maximumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumSize-prop)().\n\n**Warning:** Calling setGeometry() inside\n[resizeEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#resizeEvent)() or\n[moveEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#moveEvent)() can lead to\ninfinite recursion.\n\nSee the [Window\nGeometry](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/application-windows.html#window-geometry)\ndocumentation for an overview of geometry issues with windows.\n\nBy default, this property contains a value that depends on the user's platform and\nscreen geometry.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| const QRect \\& | **geometry**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **[setGeometry](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#setGeometry-1)**(int *x*, int *y*, int *w*, int *h*) |\n| void | **setGeometry**(*const QRect \\&*) |\n\n**See also**\n[frameGeometry](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#frameGeometry-prop)(),\n[rect](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#rect-prop)(),\n[move](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#pos-prop)(),\n[resize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#size-prop)(),\n[moveEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#moveEvent)(),\n[resizeEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#resizeEvent)(),\n[minimumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumSize-prop)(), and\n[maximumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumSize-prop)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#geometry"
    height: int
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### height : const int\n\nThis property holds the height of the widget excluding any window frame\n\nSee the [Window\nGeometry](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/application-windows.html#window-geometry)\ndocumentation for an overview of geometry issues with windows.\n\n**Note:** Do not use this function to find the height of a screen on a [multiple screen\ndesktop](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdesktopwidget.html). Read [this\nnote](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdesktopwidget.html#screen-geometry) for\ndetails.\n\nBy default, this property contains a value that depends on the user's platform and\nscreen geometry.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| int | **height**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also** [geometry](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#geometry-prop),\n[width](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#width-prop), and\n[size](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#size-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#height"
    inputMethodHints: Any
    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### inputMethodHints : [Qt::InputMethodHints](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#InputMethodHint-enum)\n\nWhat input method specific hints the widget has.\n\nThis is only relevant for input widgets. It is used by the input method to retrieve\nhints as to how the input method should operate. For example, if the\n[Qt::ImhFormattedNumbersOnly](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#InputMethodHint-enum)\nflag is set, the input method may change its visual components to reflect that only\nnumbers can be entered.\n\n**Warning:** Some widgets require certain flags in order to work as intended. To set a\nflag, do `w->setInputMethodHints(w->inputMethodHints()|f)` instead of\n`w->setInputMethodHints(f)`.\n\n**Note:** The flags are only hints, so the particular input method implementation is\nfree to ignore them. If you want to be sure that a certain type of characters are\nentered, you should also set a\n[QValidator](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qvalidator.html) on the widget.\n\nThe default value is\n[Qt::ImhNone](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#InputMethodHint-enum).\n\nThis property was introduced in Qt 4.6.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| Qt::InputMethodHints | **inputMethodHints**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setInputMethodHints**(Qt::InputMethodHints *hints*) |\n\n**See also**\n[inputMethodQuery](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#inputMethodQuery)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#inputMethodHints'
    isActiveWindow: bool
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### isActiveWindow : const bool\n\nThis property holds whether this widget's window is the active window\n\nThe active window is the window that contains the widget that has keyboard focus (The\nwindow may still have focus if it has no widgets or none of its widgets accepts keyboard\nfocus).\n\nWhen popup windows are visible, this property is `true` for both the active window *and*\nfor the popup.\n\nBy default, this property is `false`.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| bool | **isActiveWindow**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also**\n[activateWindow](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#activateWindow)() and\n[QApplication::activeWindow](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qapplication.html#activeWindow)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#isActiveWindow"
    layoutDirection: Any
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### layoutDirection : [Qt::LayoutDirection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#LayoutDirection-enum)\n\nThis property holds the layout direction for this widget.\n\n**Note:** This method no longer affects text layout direction since Qt 4.7.\n\nBy default, this property is set to\n[Qt::LeftToRight](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#LayoutDirection-enum).\n\nWhen the layout direction is set on a widget, it will propagate to the widget's\nchildren, but not to a child that is a window and not to a child for which\nsetLayoutDirection() has been explicitly called. Also, child widgets added *after*\nsetLayoutDirection() has been called for the parent do not inherit the parent's layout\ndirection.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| Qt::LayoutDirection | **layoutDirection**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setLayoutDirection**(Qt::LayoutDirection *direction*) |\n| void | **unsetLayoutDirection**() |\n\n**See also**\n[QApplication::layoutDirection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#layoutDirection-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#layoutDirection"
    locale: QLocale
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### locale : [QLocale](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlocale.html)\n\nThis property holds the widget's locale\n\nAs long as no special locale has been set, this is either the parent's locale or (if\nthis widget is a top level widget), the default locale.\n\nIf the widget displays dates or numbers, these should be formatted using the widget's\nlocale.\n\nThis property was introduced in Qt 4.3.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QLocale | **locale**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setLocale**(const QLocale \\&*locale*) |\n| void | **unsetLocale**() |\n\n**See also** [QLocale](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlocale.html) and\n[QLocale::setDefault](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlocale.html#setDefault)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#locale"
    maximized: Any
    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### maximized : const bool\n\nThis property holds whether this widget is maximized\n\nThis property is only relevant for windows.\n\n**Note:** Due to limitations on some window systems, this does not always report the\nexpected results (e.g., if the user on X11 maximizes the window via the window manager,\nQt has no way of distinguishing this from any other resize). This is expected to improve\nas window manager protocols evolve.\n\nBy default, this property is `false`.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| bool | **isMaximized**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also**\n[windowState](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#windowState)(),\n[showMaximized](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#showMaximized)(),\n[visible](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#visible-prop),\n[show](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#show)(),\n[hide](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#hide)(),\n[showNormal](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#showNormal)(), and\n[minimized](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimized-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximized'
    maximumHeight: int
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### maximumHeight : int\n\nThis property holds the widget's maximum height in pixels\n\nThis property corresponds to the height held by the\n[maximumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumSize-prop)\nproperty.\n\nBy default, this property contains a value of 16777215\\.\n\n**Note:** The definition of the `QWIDGETSIZE_MAX` macro limits the maximum size of\nwidgets.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| int | **maximumHeight**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setMaximumHeight**(int *maxh*) |\n\n**See also**\n[maximumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumSize-prop) and\n[maximumWidth](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumWidth-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumHeight"
    maximumSize: QSize
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### maximumSize : [QSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsize.html)\n\nThis property holds the widget's maximum size in pixels\n\nThe widget cannot be resized to a larger size than the maximum widget size.\n\nBy default, this property contains a size in which both width and height have values of\n16777215\\.\n\n**Note:** The definition of the `QWIDGETSIZE_MAX` macro limits the maximum size of\nwidgets.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QSize | **maximumSize**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setMaximumSize**(*const QSize \\&*) |\n| void | **[setMaximumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#setMaximumSize-1)**(int *maxw*, int *maxh*) |\n\n**See also**\n[maximumWidth](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumWidth-prop),\n[maximumHeight](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumHeight-prop),\n[minimumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumSize-prop), and\n[sizeIncrement](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#sizeIncrement-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumSize"
    maximumWidth: int
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### maximumWidth : int\n\nThis property holds the widget's maximum width in pixels\n\nThis property corresponds to the width held by the\n[maximumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumSize-prop)\nproperty.\n\nBy default, this property contains a value of 16777215\\.\n\n**Note:** The definition of the `QWIDGETSIZE_MAX` macro limits the maximum size of\nwidgets.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| int | **maximumWidth**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setMaximumWidth**(int *maxw*) |\n\n**See also**\n[maximumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumSize-prop) and\n[maximumHeight](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumHeight-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumWidth"
    minimized: Any
    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### minimized : const bool\n\nThis property holds whether this widget is minimized (iconified)\n\nThis property is only relevant for windows.\n\nBy default, this property is `false`.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| bool | **isMinimized**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also**\n[showMinimized](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#showMinimized)(),\n[visible](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#visible-prop),\n[show](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#show)(),\n[hide](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#hide)(),\n[showNormal](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#showNormal)(), and\n[maximized](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximized-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimized'
    minimumHeight: int
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### minimumHeight : int\n\nThis property holds the widget's minimum height in pixels\n\nThis property corresponds to the height held by the\n[minimumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumSize-prop)\nproperty.\n\nBy default, this property has a value of 0\\.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| int | **minimumHeight**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setMinimumHeight**(int *minh*) |\n\n**See also**\n[minimumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumSize-prop) and\n[minimumWidth](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumWidth-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumHeight"
    minimumSize: QSize
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### minimumSize : [QSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsize.html)\n\nThis property holds the widget's minimum size\n\nThe widget cannot be resized to a smaller size than the minimum widget size. The\nwidget's size is forced to the minimum size if the current size is smaller.\n\nThe minimum size set by this function will override the minimum size defined by\n[QLayout](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlayout.html). In order to unset the\nminimum size, use a value of `QSize(0, 0)`.\n\nBy default, this property contains a size with zero width and height.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QSize | **minimumSize**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setMinimumSize**(*const QSize \\&*) |\n| void | **[setMinimumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#setMinimumSize-1)**(int *minw*, int *minh*) |\n\n**See also**\n[minimumWidth](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumWidth-prop),\n[minimumHeight](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumHeight-prop),\n[maximumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#maximumSize-prop), and\n[sizeIncrement](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#sizeIncrement-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumSize"
    minimumSizeHint: QSize
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### minimumSizeHint : const [QSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsize.html)\n\nThis property holds the recommended minimum size for the widget\n\nIf the value of this property is an invalid size, no minimum size is recommended.\n\nThe default implementation of minimumSizeHint() returns an invalid size if there is no\nlayout for this widget, and returns the layout's minimum size otherwise. Most built-in\nwidgets reimplement minimumSizeHint().\n\n[QLayout](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlayout.html) will never resize a widget to\na size smaller than the minimum size hint unless\n[minimumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumSize-prop)() is set\nor the size policy is set to QSizePolicy::Ignore. If\n[minimumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumSize-prop)() is\nset, the minimum size hint will be ignored.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| virtual QSize | **minimumSizeHint**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also** [QSize::isValid](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsize.html#isValid)(),\n[resize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#size-prop)(),\n[setMinimumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumSize-prop)(),\nand [sizePolicy](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#sizePolicy-prop)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumSizeHint"
    minimumWidth: int
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### minimumWidth : int\n\nThis property holds the widget's minimum width in pixels\n\nThis property corresponds to the width held by the\n[minimumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumSize-prop)\nproperty.\n\nBy default, this property has a value of 0\\.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| int | **minimumWidth**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setMinimumWidth**(int *minw*) |\n\n**See also**\n[minimumSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumSize-prop) and\n[minimumHeight](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumHeight-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#minimumWidth"
    modal: Any
    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### modal : const bool\n\nThis property holds whether the widget is a modal widget\n\nThis property only makes sense for windows. A modal widget prevents widgets in all other\nwindows from getting any input.\n\nBy default, this property is `false`.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| bool | **isModal**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also** [isWindow](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#isWindow)(),\n[windowModality](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#windowModality-prop),\nand [QDialog](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdialog.html).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#modal'
    mouseTracking: Any
    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### mouseTracking : bool\n\nThis property holds whether mouse tracking is enabled for the widget\n\nIf mouse tracking is disabled (the default), the widget only receives mouse move events\nwhen at least one mouse button is pressed while the mouse is being moved.\n\nIf mouse tracking is enabled, the widget receives mouse move events even if no buttons\nare pressed.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| bool | **hasMouseTracking**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setMouseTracking**(bool *enable*) |\n\n**See also**\n[mouseMoveEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#mouseMoveEvent)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#mouseTracking'
    normalGeometry: QRect
    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### normalGeometry : const [QRect](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qrect.html)\n\nThis property holds the geometry of the widget as it will appear when shown as a normal\n(not maximized or full screen) top-level widget\n\nFor child widgets this property always holds an empty rectangle.\n\nBy default, this property contains an empty rectangle.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QRect | **normalGeometry**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also**\n[QWidget::windowState](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#windowState)()\nand [QWidget::geometry](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#geometry-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#normalGeometry'
